    "The survey stake is found DURING the pacing, at the third cord (sixty meters) left of the road along the line, by Brom bending to set his marker on it — a forearm's length of square iron, driven, top struck flat, standing a hand's height out of the scrub's root-tangle with the bush grown round it; examined after the count. Seln clears the roots with his knife; the registry stamp (the mark on the corner of every printed registry sheet, which Cael reads upside down before Seln says it) and a punched number, thirty-one; Seln's estimate 'Five years in the weather. A winter either side.'; Seln's professional line 'You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from.' The stake stands on the line 'to the width of a boot' by Karis's cord against Lira's stride.",
    "Seln's rule for the trials: declare inside only; if it renders they learn one thing, if not another, and only the first calls the dogs; nobody declares on the near side of the stone.",
    "Each companion's bodily failure at the line: Lira goes through the whole burst from the inside and takes one ordinary step ('It's in me. It's not in the air.'); Brom's Iron Skin declared inside does not bring the stillness Cael watches for, and Lira raps the ford-scarred forearm with her knuckles ('Skin.' / 'Skin.'); Karis sees the whole lattice laid on the air, holds her hand where the first point goes, and notes 'It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend.'; Seln walks twenty paces in and Cael, watching for it, loses him for a breath between two bushes that would not hide a dog.",
    "Oryn's trial manner: the surface reading run outside first (count of ten; 'Iron Skin. Dense. The mend's holding. Same arm it was.'); she walks Brom over the stone with her hands on the arm; she does it three times unasked; she says 'What she said. The clock.' at her first return, deferring to Lira's line rather than repeating it; she says the carters' sentence 'as a finding, to nobody'.",
    "Cael's crossing: the Iron-adjacent read released on the near side of the stone before the stride (the rut's packed edge, gravel, the stone's own weight), running on across the line; the evasion at twenty strides round a fist of ridge-stone in the grass, a foot's worth; the private sentence 'There was no dark. There was a read, and ground.' A third, permitted grace note inside the ring: the read run on the floor under his palms, giving him 'one piece of stone from his hands to the lip, no join, no seam' — he writes 'no seam' and keeps the rest.",
    "The site's specifics: the eleven uprights at their own heights (tallest to his shoulder, shortest to his knee), each broken clean across at a different place; the floor twenty-six strides across on both lines; Karis levels it by lying with her cheek on the stone and sighting along a taut cord between uprights (no daylight under it anywhere); the lip a hand's height, turned over like a basin's rim; the carved lines a fingernail deep, a knife's back wide, cut round each upright in bands, regular as a rule, 'the same kind of line and never the same line'; Karis copies them by charcoal rubbing on sheets through the afternoon; her masonry comparison is made from chips and rubbings in the middle box ('Thornwater's mortar, the ridge's stone, and the masonries she had chips of, carried out of two academies and a records hall'); her alphabet line: 'None I own. And I own more than the registry prints.'",
    "The mule and two boxes are left on the road at the stone when the six go in; Brom carries the middle box in by strap because Karis asked for it.",
    "Lira, inside the ring, sets for a burst on the floor's middle twice more and takes two ordinary steps, then sits down by Oryn and says nothing.",
    "The den's sign in Seln's reading: the round grey-dust print (the one Cael saw in the ford's mud) pressed over itself in a bare patch at the lip's foot; long bones cracked for marrow, a jaw, something with hair on it; scat a day old and no more; the hollow dug under the far lip where the fused stone stands a forearm proud of the grass, its mouth worn smooth as a doorstep; Seln's thumb in a print testing the dust's edge; 'Fresh. Today's. A lot of them.'",
    "The closing log carries a dateline inventory line before the mandated text: 'Ninety-sixth day. The Fallow Ring, inside the line, at the far lip. A hundred and eight in hand; nothing owed. Eleven uprights. One stake. Eighteen.'"
